  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to government restrictions arising from COVID-19, the Employers Confederation of the Philippines (ECOP) was unable to deliver face-to-face training, which was its main service delivery model and main source of income (approximately 22%) and experienced declining membership. In response, ECOP launched the Special Project on COVID-19 in March 2020 to improve its online training services and launched eCampus learning platform in July 2020. Through this platform, ECOP conducted a variety of remote trainings and scaled up its training offerings. 
From July 2020 through September 2021, ECOP conducted 75 e-trainings, which included tailored training addressing pressing concerns related to the business operations during the pandemic. The most noteworthy COVID-related trainings include &quot;Pandemic Preparedness and Occupational Safety and Health&quot;, &quot;How to Effectively Manage Remote Employees&quot; and &quot;Designing Climate Surveys to Assess Employee Wellbeing during the Pandemic&quot;. ECOP also rolled out programmes on soft skills, human resources management and entrepreneurship development to meet the demands of members.
During July to December 2020, ECOP conducted 53 online training programmes for 1,284 participants. Training attendance rose 76% from fiscal years 2017-2020. 
The training fee for one programme is USD 48 for ECOP members and USD 81 for non-members. Net projected monthly income per one programme is USD 1,200. 
ECOP plans to promote its training programmes to non-ECOP members with a view to attracting new members.  
In order to communicate eCampus programmes to targeted participants, ECOP made the marketing and sustainability plan and designated two specialists to collect and analyse training evaluation. To meet the increased demand and ensure the sustainability of eCampus, ECOP developed the tools for self-paced learning programmes through the eCampus platform in October 2021. This programme allows participants to access the online courses at their own speed. With the support of Walt Disney Company, the ILO and ITC-ILO assisted ECOP in establishing an eCampus platform, a Moodle type learning management system, to improve and expand the delivery of its training services. 
The ILO set up the platform and conducted training for 6 staff members of ECOP Secretariat including Director General on how to operate the platform and manage the eCampus in July 2020.
The ILO supported the development and delivery of a student-led/self-paced learning package on employment relations and international labour standards. The ILO also provided a variety of resource materials on social dialogue and international labour standards. Advice was further provided on managing and sustaining the service and digital transformation of the organization by linking Qualtrics &#x2013; an online business operating system and survey platform &#x2013; with ECOP&apos;s customer relationship management (CRM) system.</narrative>
   </description>
